{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790337730,"nonce":"6C6pxvN6sPyPFV7zi+Q8nNXdU04=","title":"Lua memory_pressure fails under heavy machine load: the short run's peak comes in low","message":"crates/zyntax_lua/tests/memory_pressure.rs, Mac debug --features llvm-backend, ZYLUA_LLVM=1 ZYNTAX_DISABLE_WARM_UP=1, on perf-integration after L-gc-semantics (tree 0044fd01 rebased onto d7500d72).\n\nTwo runs at load average 45 to 90 failed; a third at load 8 to 25 passed (154 s against 301 and 443 s). The second failure named concat.lua: 74 MB at 20000 steps, 80 MB at 400000 (limit 5 MB). Run by hand at low load, the same binary and settings give concat.lua 80.8 MB at both counts, three times. So the long run is not growing: the short run's peak is lower when the machine is loaded, most likely because it exits before background tier compiles land their code. The first failure's program was not captured.\n\nconcat.lua does not call setmetatable, so the GC package's hooks are never installed for it.\n\nNext step: make the test compare runs that reach the same tiers (wait for pending tier-ups before exit under a test switch, or measure the small run after the tiers settle), or measure the heap rather than peak RSS.","files":null}]}